PART 1: H MOD p FOR EVERY PRIME AT n=5
------------------------------------------------------------

  n=5: H values = [1, 3, 5, 9, 11, 13, 15]
  H max = 15

    p  H mod p values                  missing          why
  ───  ──────────────────────────────  ───────────────  ────────────────────────────────────────
    2  [1]                             [0]              Rédei: H always odd → H mod 2 = 1 always
    3  [0, 1, 2]                       []               No gap: all residues achievable
    5  [0, 1, 3, 4]                    [2]              α₁=3 impossible → H=1+2·3=7, 7 mod 5=2 forbidden
    7  [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6]              [0]              H=7 forbidden → 0 missing; also 7∤other H at n=5
   11  [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 9]           [6, 7, 8, 10]    H≤15 < 2·11 → limited range
   13  [0, 1, 2, 3, 5, 9, 11]          [4, 6, 7, 8, 10, 12]  H≤15 < 2·13 → limited range


